# UTC. naver datalab: monthly (basis: the keyword dictionary, contracts/entrypoints.md), day 1. 06:10 clears every
# commerce time (02:10/03:30/04:15/04:45/05:30); naver walks a different host, so the commerce gap rule
# does not bind it.
# Live again since upstream #90: every request now carries the global anchor, so a monthly pull is
# comparable with the ones before it (the rescale is db/views/naver_datalab_rescaled.sql).
10 6 1 * *  cosmai collect naver --dataset datalab
# naver blog: monthly too -- every run re-walks all 15 keyword-group terms from scratch (no cursor;
# natural-key upsert on post_id makes that safe), so once a month is enough spend. 06:40 clears datalab
# (06:10), analyze all (05:00, entrypoints.md §Schedule) and every commerce time.
40 6 1 * *  cosmai collect naver --dataset blog
# naver launch_onset (#285): monthly too, and on the same day -- the series it reads is monthly, so
# a second pass inside one month would re-ask the vendor for the same numbers. 07:20 clears blog
# (06:40) and datalab (06:10), so the three naver passes never overlap on one API Hub key; it is the
# heaviest of the three (two requests a product, ~496 against a 50,000/month ceiling) and it is the
# only one whose spend grows with the catalogue. It writes nothing at all until
# collectors/naver/launch_terms.json is filled -- the run ends blocked (2) with an empty term list.
20 7 1 * *  cosmai collect naver --dataset launch_onset
